  <field_tags rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CSG</field_tags>
  <field_tags rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CSG Cultural Recreation</field_tags>
  <field_tags rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Culture</field_tags>
  <field_wiki_entry rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The [[inst_cultural_seeding_group]], in its attempt to spread wide the many ways in which to be human, oftentimes consulted history for cultural creations, often outright reporducing cultures from human history on earth.

While the archeological and historical records ar enot without fault, the CSG attempted to recreate cultures faithfully where possible.


! Examples
!! Antiquity

() [[Cypriot-Greek Culture of Ur]]

() [[Henotikon Culture]]

!! Modern Period

() [[Weimar Republic Culture]]</field_wiki_entry>
